So I've given this a bit of thought and I think it'd be great to add an extension on to `App` supporting the same configurations supported by [`EventLoopExtDesktop`](https://docs.rs/winit/0.22.2/winit/platform/desktop/trait.EventLoopExtDesktop.html) which would allow us to configure App to return from run.

This would let us use it in tests as well as let clients of Bevy make an informed decision for their projects. I'd write similar caveats into the documentation for the new API linking to the caveats in the dependency.

@Ratysz, @cart what do you think?  If that sounds good I'd be happy to take the issue.

issue.body:
## Bevy version

0.12.1

## Relevant system information

If you cannot get Bevy to build or run on your machine, please include:

- the Rust version you're using (you can get this by running `cargo --version`)
  - cargo 1.75.0 (1d8b05cdd 2023-11-20)
- the operating system or browser used, including its version
  - MacOS 14.2.1 (M1 ARM)

## What you did

Here's a minimal version of my program:
```rust
fn main() {
        let mut app = App::new();
        app.add_plugins(DefaultPlugins.build()/*.disable::<WinitPlugin>()*/);
        app.add_systems(Update, capture_frame);
}

fn capture_frame(
    main_window: Query<Entity, With<PrimaryWindow>>,
    mut screenshot_manager: ResMut<ScreenshotManager>,
    mut exit: EventWriter<AppExit>,
) {
    eprintln!("Taking screenshot");
    screenshot_manager.save_screenshot_to_disk(main_window.single(), "/tmp/screenshot.png").expect("Failed to take screenshot to disk");
    eprintln!("Took screenshot");
    exit.send(AppExit);
```
## What went wrong

As described, `exit.send(AppExit)` shuts down the app at the start of the next scheduling tick. Unfortunately, this means the screenshot is never taken. If I remove `exit.send` the screenshot is taken.

I would sort of expect taht there would be some Drop impl that takes the screenshot on shutdown.

## Additional Information
As you might be able to guess from https://github.com/bevyengine/bevy/issues/11493 as well, my high level intention is to run a Bevy app for a single rendering frame, take a screenshot, and then exit it (and then ultimately return that data as an image via an API but that's an aside).
